# RETIRED SCAFFOLD SOURCE (SN-028). This dial now lives in
# process.toml.template -> docs/process.toml. SN-029 then RETIRED the
# three-value enum itself: the dial is `[attestation]
# human_approval_through` (a `DevStg-*` rung) plus `keep_nondependent` and
# `final_review`, and
# bootstrap.py no longer copies this file into a new repo — shipping both
# homes would hand every scaffold the mixed-config refusal. The file stays
# in the kit as the reference for the legacy vocabulary that
# `bootstrap.py --migrate-config` reads when converting an existing
# adoption; the text below describes that legacy home, not today's.
#
# Gate-authority policy (process.md §4; process-options.md "Gate authority
# levels"). One value on the last line — who approves a gate advance. Stages are
# DERIVED: docs/stage is computed from the artifact states by derive_stage.py, and
# a gate advances when a batch of artifacts is APPROVED in a reviewed commit
# (Status Draft->Planned, or an SN moved out of a draft section). This level
# governs WHO may make that approving commit:
#   attended      — a human approves each batch (the default; standard §4).
#   single-approve — LLM review through the requirement and test rungs; the human
#                   approves the queued batch once at the phase's
#                   [DevStg-Impl] close; autonomous after.
#   autonomous    — every gate except the owner's final read closes on an independent
#                   fresh-context LLM reviewer's recorded verdict.
# A non-default level is amended into the repo by the deviation register
# (docs/gate-policy.md — scaffolded by `bootstrap.py --gate-policy`); the §4
# fixed points hold at every level. This policy value is itself hand-set — change
# it in a reviewed commit (docs/stage itself is generated, never hand-edited).
attended
